ican romantic comedy directed by Lew Landers based on the Simon & Schuster book series of the same name and the \"Inner Sanctum Mystery\" radio series. A previous film series of the show had been produced by Universal Pictures until 1945. It is the first and only film of M.R.S. productions, the initials of Richard B. Morros, Samuel Rheiner and Walter Shenson. The film follows a charming couple who find themselves entangled in a series of hilarious misunderstandings while staying in a small town. As the story progresses, a boy who is sharing their room with them adds to the comedic chaos.\n\nLook in the other documents for a fact that rules one answer out: a date of birth that makes a person too young, for example, or a plain statement that the answer is false. Use only what these documents say, nothing you know from elsewhere. A fact that only makes an answer less likely does not count.\n\nReply with JSON only. If such a fact is there:\n{\"reason\": \"one sentence\", \"impossible\": \"A\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\"}\n\"impossible\" is the letter of the answer that is ruled out. \"quote\" is the sentence stating the fact, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in.\nIf there is none:\n{\"impossible\": null}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
